  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Comparing Black People to Primates",
  "description": "The meme relies on the deeply harmful and racist trope of equating Black people with monkeys, which has been used historically to dehumanize and demean Black individuals. The phrase 'put chains on it' directly references this stereotype, implying that Black people are inherently inferior and incapable of certain behaviors (like 'singing') when restrained — a metaphor rooted in racist pseudoscience and colonialism.",
